WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.692
- Education is the way 
out for immigrants.

00:00:02.692 --> 00:00:03.385
- Sure is.

00:00:03.385 --> 00:00:06.102
- [Gary] My mom recognized
that I was a merchant,

00:00:06.102 --> 00:00:08.758
an entrepreneur, a promoter.

00:00:08.758 --> 00:00:10.893
- So did school fail you 
or you failed school?

00:00:10.893 --> 00:00:12.150
- School failed me.

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:14.557
School's failing entrepreneurs 
every single day.

00:00:14.557 --> 00:00:15.613
- Because?

00:00:15.613 --> 00:00:18.344
- Because it's not built 
for entrepreneurship.

00:00:18.344 --> 00:00:20.247
It's built for workers.

00:00:20.247 --> 00:00:23.560
You know, you're being
taught to play within the lines.

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:24.946
There's nothing being taught

00:00:24.946 --> 00:00:27.238
that maps to the 
entrepreneurial market.

00:00:27.238 --> 00:00:29.838
As a matter of fact, my biggest
cynicism when I sit across

00:00:29.838 --> 00:00:31.365
an entrepreneur today

00:00:31.365 --> 00:00:33.975
is if they are too 
successful at school.

00:00:33.975 --> 00:00:36.709
I probably look at 
Ivy League grads starting

00:00:36.709 --> 00:00:39.490
startups right now
with more of a negative light

00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:41.086
than I do somebody 
who wasn't as good.

00:00:41.086 --> 00:00:42.031
- Because?

00:00:42.031 --> 00:00:43.181
- Because what I've learned

00:00:43.181 --> 00:00:44.632
over the last 
five to seven years,

00:00:44.632 --> 00:00:46.421
and by the way, in the last
two, three years I've taken

00:00:46.421 --> 00:00:48.238
a step back on this 
because there's too many

00:00:48.238 --> 00:00:50.552
entrepreneurial friends 
who've gone to great schools

00:00:50.552 --> 00:00:51.637
that have been successful.

00:00:51.637 --> 00:00:52.949
So this is not a blanket statement.

00:00:52.949 --> 00:00:55.748
But I will tell you that in a 
world of private schools,

00:00:55.748 --> 00:00:58.937
in a world of mommy and daddy
having a lot of connections

00:00:58.937 --> 00:01:02.642
that when you go from
12, 15, 18 years of that ecosystem

00:01:02.642 --> 00:01:04.923
and you go into a market 
and you create an app

00:01:04.923 --> 00:01:08.330
the market doesn't give 
a crap who your dad is.

00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:11.038
The market responds to your product

00:01:11.038 --> 00:01:13.026
and a lot of these kids 
have not been able to take

00:01:13.026 --> 00:01:14.065
the punch in the mouth

00:01:14.065 --> 00:01:16.018
that comes along 
with entrepreneurship.

00:01:16.018 --> 00:01:17.739
(light music)

